// The creaturerig package: any creature's skeleton from data, and the
// weights that bind a mesh to it. A program reaches it with 'import
// creaturerig'.
//
// - RigSpec (spec.cone): a skeleton as plain data. Named chains (spine,
//   neck, head, tail, leg, wing, arm, feather, or a kind of the program's
//   own) of bones, each with a rest offset and a radius, hung from a bone of
//   another chain. Any number of each; none is special. 'mirror' makes the
//   other side of a limb. parse.cone reads the same data from text.
// - Rig (rig.cone): the spec built into a bonepose Skeleton ('buildRig'),
//   with the chains found by name or kind, each bone's name, radius and
//   rest place. This is what leggedgait and wingflight take.
// - Weights (weights.cone): how a mesh is bound to the bones. 'heatWeights'
//   is the bone-heat method (Baran and Popovic, "Automatic rigging and
//   animation of 3D characters", SIGGRAPH 2007, the method of Pinocchio and
//   of Blender's automatic weights): weights spread over the surface from
//   each bone by diffusion, so a leg's skin follows its own leg and not the
//   one a hand's breadth away across the gap. 'envelopeWeights' is the
//   plain distance method, for comparison and for meshes too big to solve.
//   'skinPositions' is linear blend skinning on the CPU, the twin of
//   render's skinning.slang.
// - Text (parse.cone): 'parseRig' reads a rig from lines of text.
//
// Conventions are bonepose's: metres, right handed, y up, the creature faces
// -z, its right is +x. The package imports bonepose, geomath, mesh and
// collections, and nothing that draws: render's Skin is made from a
// VertexWeights by the program that draws (four joints and four weights a
// vertex, the same shape).
//
//   creaturerig.cone   this overview
//   spec.cone          BoneSpec, ChainSpec, RigSpec, the kinds
//   rig.cone           Chain, Rig, buildRig
//   weights.cone       heatWeights, envelopeWeights, skinPositions
//   parse.cone         parseRig
//   samples.cone       plainBody: generic test bodies of any number of legs, with or without neck, tail, wings

mod creaturerig;

import libc;
import collections use *;
import geomath use *;
import bonepose use *;
import mesh use Mesh;
